    section: "B", questionRef: "2011 HL Section B Q5(b)",
    stem: "Families are the oldest expression of human relationship and have been continually adapting to change, human development and progress.",
    questionText: "Discuss the roles and responsibilities of family members and explain how these roles change through the life cycle of the family.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"fixed","notation":"6 points @ 4"}, totalMarks: 24,
    rows: [
    { id: "points", kind: "criterion", verbatim: "roles and responsibilities", marks: 24, contextNote: "Distinct source points at the printed value; no finer marking ladder is published. Complete source guidance: Children’s Roles and Responsibilities Son/daughter/brother/sister/grandchild. Responsibilities influenced by age but include showing respect, learning to behave in a socially acceptable manner, acquiring knowledge informally and formally, achieving gradual independence. Adolescents May have extra responsibilities babysitting, helping younger children with homework, contributing to decision making and running of the home. Parents’ Roles and Responsibilities Mother/Father/Spouse Reproduction; Nurturing; Socialisation; economic; education; caring for each other; caring for the elderly. Grandparents’ Roles and Responsibilities Grandparent/spouse As people tend to live longer nowadays and are generally in good health, they play a prominent role in family life. Spending time with their children/grandchildren; childcare; financial help for their families; emotional support for children/grandchildren; passing on values e.g. respect and life experiences etc.", permittedMarks: [0,4,8,12,16,20,24], parts: [{"id":"point-1","verbatim":"Point 1","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]},{"id":"point-2","verbatim":"Point 2","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]},{"id":"point-3","verbatim":"Point 3","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]},{"id":"point-4","verbatim":"Point 4","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]},{"id":"point-5","verbatim":"Point 5","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]},{"id":"point-6","verbatim":"Point 6","marks":4,"permittedMarks":[0,4]}] },
    ],
